Let \(I=\{x:Cx\le d\}\) and \(x\in I\). Then
\[N_I(x)=\{C^T\lambda:\lambda\ge0,\ \lambda_i(C_ix-d_i)=0\ \forall i\}
=\operatorname{cone}\{C_i^T:C_ix=d_i\}.\]

When \(0<\theta\le\tfrac12\), the KL inequality, relative error, and quadratic sufficient decrease yield constants \(C,C'>0\), \(q\in(0,1)\), and \(k_0\) such that \[r_k\le Cq^k,
\qquad \|x_k-\bar x\|\le C' q^{k/2}
\qquad(k\ge k_0).\] Thus the objective residual is geometrically decreasing, and the iterates converge at least R-linearly after a harmless change of contraction factor.
